> Not sure what {tai} does here, no NP after it.

{tai} is a selbri tag there, which means it implicitly tags {zo'e}.

> (I pass over {ci'omle},
> you're entitle to make your compounds mean whatever you want them to.)

{ci'omle} is an alternate form of {citmle}, which has been in the 
dictionary for a long time, but some prefer the sound of {ci'omle}. Both 
mean "cute". I guess I'll add {ci'omle} as well, didn't know it hadn't 
already been added.

